. esrtest, pdid

Pseudo-DiD on the selection index (H0: no selection on gains, kappa = 0)
(strata of the probit index Z'g; X-adjusted gap treated - untreated within each)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
stratum |    n1     n0   mean P |     gap  Std. err. | mean lambda1  mean lambda0
--------+----------------------+--------------------+--------------------------
    1   |    89    516    0.139 |  0.1999     0.0349 |       1.5392        0.2593
    2   |   164    441    0.270 |  0.1530     0.0252 |       1.1867        0.4485
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  double difference of the gaps, top - bottom:     -0.0469  (s.e. 0.0432)
  within treated,   top - bottom (C1):             0.0836  (s.e. 0.0433, z =   1.93)   sign of rho1*sigma1 = sign(C1/pi1
> ), pi1 = -0.246
  within untreated, top - bottom (C0):             0.0979  (s.e. 0.0269, z =   3.64)   sign of rho0*sigma0 = -sign(C0/pi
> 0), pi0 =  0.126
  rho1*sigma1 = C1/pi1 =  -0.3401 (s.e. 0.1798)    rho0*sigma0 = -C0/pi0 =  -0.7795 (s.e. 0.3000)
  kappa_dd =   0.4394  (s.e. 0.3197, z =   1.37)     esreg kappa =   0.2102 (s.e. 0.1523)
pi_j: the X-adjusted contrast of the Mills ratio lambda_j, top - bottom, in group j (the same
regression as C_j with lambda_j for y).
Std. err.: influence function of the whole procedure (probit, boundaries of the strata, regressions).
note: the boundary between strata 1 and 2 sits on tied values of the index (1.4%
  of the sample at one value), which a resample can move as a block: the standard errors
  of the gaps, of the double difference and, less so, of C1 and C0 are approximate
  (kappa_dd resists: C_j and pi_j move together); reps(#) gives the bootstrap of the whole procedure.
note: the Mills contrast pi1 has a coefficient of variation of 23%: rho1*sigma1 = C1/pi1
  and kappa_dd are far from normal and their standard errors approximate; read the sign of C1, or use reps(#).
note: the Mills contrast pi0 has a coefficient of variation of 29%: rho0*sigma0 = -C0/pi0
  and kappa_dd are far from normal and their standard errors approximate; read the sign of C0, or use reps(#).
Reading: with kappa > 0 the gap falls across the strata (the eager treated at low P gain
more, the reluctant untreated at high P would have gained less); the signs of C1 and C0 need
only A2; kappa_dd uses the Mills ratios of A1. Never split on the outcome itself (collider).

